menu "VoxConductor voice"
config VOX_LOG_VERBOSE
    bool "Detailed serial diagnostics"
    default n
    help
        Normal mode prints short voice turn IDs, a bounded transcript preview,
        playback/result summaries and essential warnings/errors. Wake status
        is printed every 15 seconds instead of every 2 seconds.
        Enable for per-phase heap/timing, full dialogue text (if permitted by
        APP_TURN_LOG_TEXT), model/tool internals and vendor INFO logs.
        Console verbosity changes here; SD records and device behavior stay unchanged.
config VOX_WAKE_WORD
    bool "Build experimental local idle wake-word recognition"
    default n
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
    help
        Select the bundled Chinese 小冰小冰 model (wn9_xiaobinxiaobin_tts) in
        ESP Speech Recognition and use partitions_wake.csv. Flash the model
        partition as well as firmware, using the bundled model path.
        Select a trained model for the desired wake word.
        Runtime opt-in is also required in the device Settings menu.
        Idle microphone audio stays on the device. After wake, wait for
        the Listening screen before speaking. Recording ends on silence.
config VOX_WAKE_MODEL_NAME
    string "Exact WakeNet model name"
    depends on VOX_WAKE_WORD
    default "wn9_xiaobinxiaobin_tts"
    help
        The bundled model recognizes 小滨小滨 / 小冰小冰.
        Use the real model name provided with a replacement trained model.
        Empty or missing names keep wake-word recognition unavailable. Never choose
        wn9_customword as a placeholder: that bundled model means Xiao Ai
        Tong Xue; a custom phrase requires a matching trained model.
config VOX_WAKE_GAIN
    int "Wake-only microphone PCM gain"
    depends on VOX_WAKE_WORD
    range 1 16
    default 1
    help
        Linear gain after DC removal, applied only to local WakeNet input.
        Cloud recording, speaker volume and model threshold keep their own settings.
        Start at 1 (no amplification). Use wake_diag raw/processed
        peaks and clip counts to calibrate; too much gain also boosts noise.
        A value of 1 disables amplification but keeps DC removal.
config VOX_WAKE_THRESHOLD_PERCENT
    int "小冰小冰 wake detection threshold (%)"
    depends on VOX_WAKE_WORD
    range 40 95
    default 60
    help
        WakeNet's public detection threshold, applied at creation and reset.
        Use a 60 percent trial threshold; validate misses and false wakes on hardware.
        The previous 55 percent trial can falsely wake on ordinary speech.
        Lower values can help missed wakes but also increase false wakes.
        Higher values reject more audio but may miss real wake words.
        Verify both quiet-room and background-speech behavior before use.
        Microphone gain and cloud recognition keep their separate settings.
config VOX_ACOUSTIC_BARGE_IN
    bool "小冰小冰 wake-word interruption during assistant playback"
    default y
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3 && SPIRAM && VOX_WAKE_WORD
    help
        Feed echo-cleaned microphone audio to the existing 小冰小冰 model.
        Only a detected wake word cancels playback; generic speech/noise never
        pauses an answer. Preserve recent audio and the following question in
        PSRAM while the old TTS connection is released, then start the next ASR.
        Reuse the existing model and keep idle audio processing local.
        Speaker playback remains 24 kHz; the echo reference uses 16 kHz.
        Button cancellation remains available and takes priority.
        Echo delay and recognition must be checked on the assembled device.
config VOX_AEC_DELAY_MS
    int "Speaker reference delay (ms)"
    depends on VOX_ACOUSTIC_BARGE_IN
    range 0 200
    default 40
config VOX_AUTO_END_SILENCE_MS
    int "Silence before ending a wake/follow-up recording (ms)"
    range 600 3000
    default 800
    help
        Local end-of-utterance tail. 800 ms shortens question-to-answer delay
        without changing microphone gain or wake-word sensitivity. Increase
        this if pauses inside a sentence are being cut into separate turns.
config VOX_AUTO_END_VAD_MODE
    int "Automatic recording VAD aggressiveness"
    range 0 3
    default 0
    help
        ESP-SR voice activity detector. 0 is most sensitive; higher values
        reject more noise but can miss quiet speech. Only automatic capture
        uses this detector; button recording still ends on release.
endmenu
